          "summary": "This memo from ISO-NE presents a proposed methodology for calculating seasonal payment rates under CAR-SA (the Capacity Auction with Seasonal Accreditation), which will replace Net CONE in transforming demand MRI curves to priced-demand curves. The method uses two assumptions—Annual Cost Equivalence and Constant Capacity Demand Curve Scaling Factor—to derive summer and winter payment rates that reflect both cost recovery for new entrants and the relative reliability value of capacity across seasons. An interim approach using existing FCA Net CONE values is required through the 2031 auction cycle until CONE and Net CONE are fully updated.",
